# GPU and eval workflow

## Preflight (before any VLM / Habitat / Robocasa GPU job)

```bash
uv run emet eval status                # see free VRAM + compute apps
uv run emet eval kill-stale
NEED_MIB=12000 uv run emet eval wait   # or: uv run emet eval check
```

Canonical CLI: **`emet eval {status,check,wait,kill-stale}`**. Bash [`scripts/gpu_preflight.sh`](../../scripts/gpu_preflight.sh) delegates to it (also provides `emet_export_pytorch_alloc` and **`emet_pytest_no_sim_ignore_args`** when sourced). Prefer `emet eval` over raw `pkill` / ad-hoc kills. Verify with `uv run emet eval --help` before suggesting flags.

## Experiment reliability

- New eval/sim `Popen` paths must use [`emet.utils.process_tree`](../../src/emet/utils/process_tree.py) (`popen_session` + `terminate_process_tree` / `kill_process_tree`) so timeouts reap GPU grandchildren (`uv` wrappers, mujoco/habitat workers).
- Do **not** run `emet eval kill-stale` from inside a long-running smoke that must stay alive (e.g. `run_dynagraph_dynamic_*`) — use `emet eval wait` only. Set `EMET_GPU_PROTECT_PIDS` if an orchestrator must keep a worker across cleanup.
- After failed/hung evals: `uv run emet eval status`, then check **`~/runs/emet/`**, **`~/.cache/habitat_eqa/results/`**, and per-step logs before re-launching.
- Docs: [`docs/evaluation.md`](../../docs/evaluation.md), orphan section in [`docs/known_issues.md`](../../docs/known_issues.md).

## `emet jobs` (required for long GPU / paper runs)

**Always** launch multi-episode Habitat/HM-EQA, overnight batteries, and paper sweeps through the job registry — not bare `nohup` when avoidable:

```bash
uv run emet jobs run --name hmeqa-agentic-bal32 --need-mib 12000 -- \
  env EMET_ALLOW_SDPA_ATTN=1 ./scripts/run_hmeqa_agentic_h2h.sh …
uv run emet jobs                 # list + PROGRESS/ETA columns
uv run emet jobs status JOB_ID   # detail + derived ETA (--json includes progress)
uv run emet jobs logs JOB_ID --tail 80
uv run emet jobs cancel JOB_ID
```

- Registry: `~/runs/emet/jobs/` (`EMET_JOBS_DIR`). Wrapper sets `EMET_JOB_ID`.
- Progress: scripts should `emet jobs update JOB_ID --units-done N --units-total M --phase … --current-id …` and/or write `OUT/progress.json` (see `emet.utils.job_registry`).
- If a job was started unmanaged: `emet jobs register` + point `--out-dir` at the run so `progress.json` / DONE are visible.
- Implementation: [`src/emet/utils/job_registry.py`](../../src/emet/utils/job_registry.py), CLI in [`docs/cli.md`](../../docs/cli.md).

## One GPU job at a time

Do **not** stack in one uninterrupted session:

- Robocasa dynagraph explore (track 4)
- Full `pytest src/test -m "not sim"` without ignore list
- Habitat HM-EQA with Qwen3-VL-8B
- `run_overnight_eval_smoke.sh`

That sequence caused full-system freezes on an RTX 4090 workstation (GUI + SSH unresponsive; mouse still moved).

| Orchestrator | Default | Notes |
|--------------|---------|-------|
| `run_simulation_smoke_battery.sh` | sequential | **Paper-facing** seven-track battery — see `docs/simulation_testing_plan.md` |
| `run_overnight_cross_track_smoke.sh` | `RUN_DEEP_EVAL=0` | Extended overnight + tier 0 + safe pytest |
| `run_overnight_eval_smoke.sh` | separate night | HM-EQA + OVMM + SQA3D matrix |
| `run_overnight_habitat_eval.sh` | `--resume` | Multi-phase HM-EQA subsets |

## Cursor agent sessions

- Run **multi-hour** Habitat evals and overnight scripts via **`uv run emet jobs run --name … -- CMD`** (or a dedicated terminal) — **not** as blocking inline commands in long agent turns.
- Monitor progress/ETA with **`emet jobs`** / **`emet jobs status`**, not only `tail` on orchestrator logs.
- If the agent segfaults mid-eval, check artifacts under **`~/runs/emet/`**, **`~/.cache/habitat_eqa/results/`**, and **`/tmp/unified_smoke_*.log`** — subprocesses may have finished.
- Tier 0 + tracks 1–3 PR smoke: see [`docs/experiments/cross_track_smoke.md`](../../docs/experiments/cross_track_smoke.md).

## Cross-track smoke entrypoint

```bash
uv run emet jobs run --name overnight-cross-track --need-mib 12000 -- \
  ./scripts/run_overnight_cross_track_smoke.sh
uv run emet jobs logs JOB_ID --tail 40
# or: tail -f ~/runs/emet/overnight_cross_track/cross_track_*/summary.txt
```

## Unified config smoke (post–PR #68)

When touching config loader or `configs/emet/default.yaml`:

```bash
uv run emet test src/test/config/ -q
uv run python -c "
from emet.core.parameters import get_parameters
p = get_parameters('dynav_innate_mars.yaml')
assert str(p.get('depth_source')).lower() == 'auto'
"
```

See [`docs/emet_config.md`](../../docs/emet_config.md).
